<title>ISRAEL: Israeli anti-trust chief resigns after five years.</title>
<headline>Israeli anti-trust chief resigns after five years.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yoram Turbowicz is resigning as Israel's commissioner for restrictive business practices effective in February 1997, the Industry and Trade Ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>He will be replaced by David Tadmor, a Tel Aviv attorney and Tel Aviv University lecturer.</p>
<p>Turbowicz has held the post since December 1991. Tadmor's appointment is subject to cabinet approval.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
</text>
